{"id": "EUVD-2026-82026", "enisaUuid": "0fea4de7-3b49-38c7-b86d-7970abf86166", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: cancel reset and rc work on device unregister\n\nBoth drivers cancelled dump_work on unregister but left reset_work and\nrc_work to be flushed only by destroy_workqueue() in mt76_free_device(),\nwhich runs after the hw is unregistered and the hardware stopped. A\nreset_work that fires in that window calls ieee80211_restart_hw() and\nre-arms mac_work on an unregistered hw, and rc_work touches station state\nbeing torn down. Cancel both up front, alongside dump_work.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5dd845c6388c6c9a4085ecdf59c7fe7bf3398e2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b3b1b3c7d434b5c5bc8d7de0b9c335242eeefba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aca0cd273b486a078f936b3fb409e619673521b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4dc85481d38951ca7f8bc104e711936306cc664", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e995d3dccc9d980af13a60ad37409ed1561f9eeb"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mg5m-xfw2-63jw", "CVE-2026-90365"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "116bb68b-1a24-32cb-b109-1cbb8a9d19d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e57b7901469fc0b021930b83a8094baaf3d81b09 <c4dc85481d38951ca7f8bc104e711936306cc664"}, {"id": "1447a79a-a101-3dd5-aa6a-24c18b8db6be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e57b7901469fc0b021930b83a8094baaf3d81b09 <e995d3dccc9d980af13a60ad37409ed1561f9eeb"}, {"id": "1c20d4ee-75df-36f7-9b2f-095cfc9e1aa1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "29f0b14a-74a4-3af2-b38a-05bae0b4aca5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "3f12f22f-8d2b-3af7-8034-2a642cb